# Principal architect checkpoint B3b: APPROVED

B3b is approved at artifacts.py SHA `33a124043338d834fe3b60508b533c777df5c4fefbbdfb52ac812ab5eda0ca4f` and runtime.py SHA `1c4c4dd2a3c7082982866e6ed820336e5afeb9755b0005fb80e65224bcc0d462`. No actionable findings were identified in the exact diff and affected call paths.

The shared validator authenticates and strictly decodes every referenced event before routing. The reserved rendering failure code, a decoded rejection event, or a rejection-payload substitution selects the strict branch independently of record status. That branch requires one sole canonical event-file reference and authenticates its exact membership in the current round journal. Corrected B2 then supplies predecessor/state/accepted-author/full-hypothesis/bounded-assignment/critic-exclusion authority. The record is compared with the actual intent, author template and rejection payload, including mode/scope and parent fingerprint fields that are not supplied by the experiment hash alone. Valid open prefixes remain usable; cleanup or critic completion is not required to append an invalid record.

Append and load both use the same validator, and ordinary records avoid unnecessary journal loading. Repository failures do not fall through into the legacy path. The existing invalid-record dataclass invariants still exclude downstream evidence. Record-backed projection recovery/publication inherit the validation through load_experiment; load_checkpoint by itself remains an envelope read. No record-to-journal recursion was introduced.

_publish validates supported candidate types, duplicate candidate IDs, and record identity/status pairing before record persistence. Only checked materialized candidates for evaluated/zero_trade records can supply source authority. Rejected records can remain in history/checkpoint references without candidate materialization or archive authority. The upstream independent expected-record equality gate remains intact.

Principal verification: `principal-architect-verification.json`. Source and preimage hashes, narrowed changed/added functions, scoped Ruff, in-memory compilation and exact-preimage diff checks passed. The unchanged 56-file evaluator identity is `005064e57e80840f3b2a97d7db694b176832b8f982996e63efc8a35064505ed4`. The historical runtime-04 evaluated record loaded with unchanged canonical bytes/hash, four discovery episodes and its critic binding. This verifies that real legacy input only. Rejection append/load/publication branches remain statically reviewed and unexecuted.

Next implement B4a only: connect rendering outcomes to durable rejection evidence and route the explicit candidate union through screening/discovery and the critic filter. Then return for review. B4b will handle no-testable lifecycle completion and finalized-campaign/recovery authority; B4c will expose bounded rejection feedback and audit retained novelty/history. Keep all campaigns stopped until those pieces and the future run's budget/readiness are reviewed.

Current code inspection clarifies an earlier broad audit note: _completed_result itself checks record/checkpoint authority and cleanup, with no direct critic requirement. It should be audited with recovery for B4b, not changed merely because its name appeared in the plan. _verify_finalized_discovery_rounds does have explicit rendered-only IDs and a mandatory three-role tuple that B4b must address.

No production edits, tests, synthetic probes, credentials, external calls, candidate evaluations, campaigns, commits, pushes or deployment occurred during this review. The original two real evaluated feedback rounds remain unfinished.
